 | `snapshot` |                           | `{"ok": true, "count": n}`                 |
 
 Keys are non-empty strings; values are any JSON value. `incr` treats a missing
 key as 0 and fails with `wrong_type` when the value is not an integer.
 
+`ttl` is a positive number of seconds. A key set at `t` with `ttl` T expires at
+`t + T` (store clock) and then behaves like a missing key everywhere. `set`
+without `ttl` clears the expiry; `incr` keeps it. `stats` reports `get`/`mget`
+hits and misses, the number of keys that expired (each once) and live keys;
+counters are not saved in snapshots.
+
 ## Python API
 
